      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 5.0,
      "text": "Here's a thing, they do not put in survival manuals."
    },
    {
      "start": 6.16,
      "end": 8.82,
      "text": "Sometimes help arrives looking badly organized."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.14,
      "end": 15.04,
      "text": "One glove, three opinions of boat hook held the wrong way round."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.9,
      "end": 19.34,
      "text": "Beautiful, honestly."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.98,
      "end": 25.02,
      "text": "I had been rowing with one useful thought and one plank"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.02,
      "end": 30.52,
      "text": "that made accusations the sea kept giving me employee feedback and buckets."
    },
    {
      "start": 30.9,
      "end": 34.9,
      "text": "Needs improvement, poor team work unsuitable footwear."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.54,
      "end": 42.06,
      "text": "Then through the morning came a little skiff with two old fishes and a child beating in pairs."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.2,
      "end": 46.42,
      "text": "No trumpets, no grand rescue posture."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.94,
      "end": 52.76,
      "text": "Just a woman with a scarf saying you look like a man who has argued with a wave and lost the minutes."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.76,
      "end": 54.86,
      "text": "Which was specific and fair."
    },
    {
      "start": 55.56,
      "end": 60.4,
      "text": "I had learned to call the empty my only honest crew."
    },
    {
      "start": 60.74,
      "end": 65.84,
      "text": "Then someone tossed in or across and said we roll this stretch too."
    },
    {
      "start": 66.48,
      "end": 71.64,
      "text": "Past the old pool together, not every mercy needs good weather."
    },
    {
      "start": 72.12,
      "end": 77.02,
      "text": "And by hand we crossed the swell, no one has to roll it wet."
    },
    {
      "start": 77.46,
      "end": 82.64,
      "text": "Past the old furth mine, the splinter, share the bread, forgive the wind."
    },
    {
      "start": 82.64,
      "end": 88.28,
      "text": "If the boat keeps moving through that is enough for me and you."
    },
    {
      "start": 89.54,
      "end": 95.7,
      "text": "Also, the child offered me half a pair with the solemn confidence of a tiny dog master."
    },
    {
      "start": 96.84,
      "end": 99.6,
      "text": "I accepted, obviously."
    },
    {
      "start": 100.24,
      "end": 106.8,
      "text": "Yeah, they did not ask for my whole sad inventory, no clipboard, no moral at the report."
    },
    {
      "start": 107.22,
      "end": 109.08,
      "text": "Can you sit up? Can you drink?"
    },
    {
      "start": 109.08,
      "end": 110.6,
      "text": "Do you know where you are?"
    },
    {
      "start": 111.0,
      "end": 112.2,
      "text": "And I said mostly."
    },
    {
      "start": 112.72,
      "end": 117.56,
      "text": "Because honesty is important for panic does not mean extra admin."
    },
    {
      "start": 118.04,
      "end": 122.32,
      "text": "The old man laughed like a rope coming loose."
    },
    {
      "start": 123.04,
      "end": 127.6,
      "text": "He said nobody knows where they are after a bad crossing."
    },
    {
      "start": 127.9,
      "end": 131.86,
      "text": "You learn by row, we next to someone for a while then he pointed at the link"
    },
    {
      "start": 131.86,
      "end": 138.16,
      "text": "with professional disappointment handed me a cup, great group bailing I thought I had to burn the deck."
    },
    {
      "start": 138.16,
      "end": 146.76,
      "text": "I never needing room, but kindness came with wet boots on and made a little room."
    },
    {
      "start": 147.46,
